hi  welcome to another episode of cold  fusion where i cover anything in science  technology business or history on march  29th 2022 cnn launched cnn plus a  venture that was going to be the future  of the company it was a  subscription-based digital platform with  a one billion dollar budget over four  years  but the entire venture catastrophically  collapsed in just three weeks  so what happened and what can we learn  here let's take a look  you are watching cold fusion tv  founded in 1980 cnn has traditionally  been the network that viewers turned to  in times of war terrorism or major news  but after 40 years things have started  to change  cnn's core news business has been  failing spectacularly in february of  2022 the company lost 70 percent of its  primetime viewers in its key demographic  this comes at a time when trust and  media is at its all-time low dropping  from 76 in 2016 down to 58 in 2021  not only this but there's been multiple  scandals involving key cnn staff from  affairs to child abuse the pressure was  too much for ceo jeff zucker and he was  forced to resign earlier this year  so how was cnn going to turn all of this  around the world was moving towards  streaming platforms so why not cnn  besides they're the biggest name in news  what could possibly go wrong  cnn is an icon of the cable and  satellite age but now cable is competing  with streaming and there isn't a  streaming subscription service for tv  news in the united states so if you were  creating a news product from scratch in  2022 how would you build it that's one  of the questions one of the starting  points for cnn plus the result was cnn  plus  what followed was a multi-million dollar  ad campaign millions more were spent on  hiring staff to produce exclusive  content  in total 300 million dollars was spent  building up the service  for viewers the subscription cost was  six dollars per month  the problems visibly began to be evident  with the branding of cnn plus a lot of  viewers thought the service was mostly  going to be exclusive live news but in  reality it was a bit of a mixed bag  although the focus was news cnn plus's  lineup included a cooking show a book  club show with jake tapper a show about  past movie stars another show about the  singer dione warwick and an anderson  cooper program about the challenges of  being a dad  frankly nobody cared about these things  but that was just the start of the  trouble  interestingly according to the new york  times it looks as if cnn plus may have  been thrown under the bus internally  you see just before the launch of cnn  plus cnn who was owned by warner media  was going through massive changes  warner brothers and hence warner media  was undergoing a merge with the  discovery company  and the thing is both companies already  had ventures in the streaming world  discovery had the discovery plus  streaming service and warner media had  hbo max  both of these streaming services were  about to be bundled into one leaving no  room for poor cnn plus  discovery executives were all skeptical  of cnn plus from the beginning in fact  before its launch the discovery managers  refused to have meetings with the cnn  plus officials to even hear what the  product was about  and this didn't happen just once this  happened three times  they just didn't care about it  internal problems aside the project was  a complete flop  executives expected 2 million  subscribers in the first year but cnn  plus only managed 10 000 consistent  viewers after the first two weeks and  that was even after lowering the price  when david zaslov the new ceo of the  warner brothers discovery merger saw the  abysmal numbers for the first time he  was appalled he made the decision to  shut it down instantly  to him cnn plus was taking up a lot of  resources and giving nothing in return  in total after 300 million dollars spent  the service was only around for three  weeks and the explosion left a trail of  destruction in its wake layoffs ensued  and the disaster upended the careers of  many would-be hopefuls this is going to  be our last episode of the source on cnn  plus it's just a few weeks after we  launched  cassie hunt who left a job at msnbc for  cnn plus stated that some of her staff  left stable jobs and some moved across  the country and she noted that all of  them took a huge risk  [Music]  so why did nobody watch all the focus  groups and surveys may have told cnn  managers that the idea was valid but  watching content for free in a  controlled setting is different from  having to pay for it  cnn although a large legacy brand  doesn't really mean all that much  anymore they aren't as important as they  were in the 1980s and 90s the market  just didn't think that the programming  on cnn plus was enough value when  compared to free tv other internet  content or other streaming platforms for  that matter  apple tv peacock disney plus paramount  plus hbo max netflix and hulu all make  for stiff competition  cnn plus was just another six dollars a  month for politics and b grade content  it was too little too late  cnn executives struggle to navigate a  rapidly changing market a market where  consumer habits are unstable and this  all just shows what happens when you get  it wrong  so let's take a look at some lessons as  i said in my episode about the failure  of quibby criticizing is easy but  building is hard  that being said what are some lessons  here here are four quick ones  the first lesson would have been don't  lean on brand recognition alone there's  no guarantee of that working especially  in a rapidly evolving market  the second lesson is obvious make better  content that appeals to the target  audience although that's much easier  said than done  number three build trust if cnn plus was  to succeed they would first have to get  the fundamentals right they would need  to build brand trust among all americans  not just 50 of them  for this to happen there would need to  be as close to unbiased reporting as  possible each story should show the  complete picture and not substitute fact  for opinion  for the what about is out there this  isn't just a cnn problem the same goes  for fox news 2 but the topic here is  obviously cnn  and the fourth and final lesson clearer  internal communication may have also  helped prevent this disaster discovery  and warner media had their own plans for  streaming services so when it became  clear that the merger was happening the  cnn plus content should have been  absorbed into the existing services  instead of limping along as a standalone  service  the lack of internal communication and  friction prevented cnn plus from being  integrated well into the wider business  plan of both parent companies  so all in all the cnn brand may have  been hurt badly by this i'd even bet  that more people have heard of the cnn  plus disaster than cnn plus itself the  whole saga leaves a question mark over  cnn's digital presence at a time when  americans are stopping to watch cable tv  so what do you guys think did you even  hear about cnn plus  it really is a cutthroat environment in  the streaming world even netflix is  starting to struggle as we're going to  see in the next episode  so before i go just some quick  housekeeping i talked about this saga  and much more in the latest episode of  my podcast which you can check out in  the description below  i also just passed 5 000 followers on  spotify for my music so thanks to  everyone who's taken a listen  anyway that's it from me  my name is dagogo and you've been  watching cold fusion and i'll catch you  again soon for the next episode  cheers guys  have a  good oh  [Music]  [Laughter]  [Music]  cold fusion  it's new thinking

